// A generic's type parameter used as a VALUE inside its body. The template is never instantiated, so
// this is the uninstantiated-template probe reporting it — a type parameter is wrong as a value at every
// instantiation, which is exactly the class of defect the probe exists to report (not to defer).
fn T pick<T>(T a) { return T; }   // ERROR: `T` is a type parameter, not a value
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
